<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;
&lt;c&gt;
use xxx (); #imports all of the symbols in @EXPORT
use xxx qw(OpenConnection $LoggedOn_user_id); # imports
 # all of the symbols in @EXPORT AND subroutine OpenConnection
 # AND the scalar $LoggedOn_user_id from @EXPORT_OK
&lt;/c&gt;
&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sorry, but those two are incorrect. As per [doc://use], &lt;c&gt;use Foo ();&lt;/c&gt; is exactly equivalent to &lt;c&gt;BEGIN { require Foo }&lt;/c&gt;, so nothing is exported at all. When you say &lt;c&gt;use Foo qw/bar/;&lt;/c&gt;, [doc://Exporter] exports only that, regardless of what's in &lt;c&gt;@EXPORT&lt;/c&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;&lt;i&gt;Update:&lt;/i&gt; Hm, my posting seems to have overlapped with an update to the node.&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
